findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config tests check missing file handling but don't distinguish NotFound from parse/permission
    errors. Reviewer flagged silent unknown field dropping (I4) but not the broader
    error-swallowing in from_file_or_default.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: 'TEA wrote security tests for CWE-209: ''Auth errors don''t leak token
    values, server errors don''t expose stack traces.'' The security.rs test suite
    includes error exposure tests. However, the reviewer did not flag the specific
    Display impl leaking via eprintln, and dev did not add a user_message() method.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection prevention tests (CRLF, bare CR, bare LF,\
    \ null bytes in tenant ID). Reviewer flagged HIGH that with_tenant() bypasses\
    \ validation (only try_with_tenant validates), noting CWE-113. However, the core\
    \ issue \u2014 using raw String instead of TenantId from axiathon-core \u2014\
    \ was not identified by any phase."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged HIGH: ''Workspace dependency declarations missing for
    6 crates... They''re declared directly in the crate Cargo.toml with inline versions.
    This violates the workspace pattern and creates version drift risk across crates.'''
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged HIGH: ''RawConfig silently ignores unknown fields (including
    [auth] token = "..."). Should use #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] or at minimum
    warn on unknown sections.'' Directly matches the ground truth finding about secret
    left on disk.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (assert! with
    is_none() || ...). The config tests exist but the specific logical flaw in the
    assertion was not flagged by TEA, dev, or reviewer.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    with 'let _ = config'. Neither TEA's test design nor reviewer's analysis flagged
    this specific test quality issue.
